WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.420 align:start position:0%
 
Wow  [Music]  valiant hearts the Great War is one of  the most human and sensitive games about  war ever released set during World War  one the game is more about the personal  struggles of its characters than it is  about the larger historical details and  political realities of the devastating  conflict the game takes a few small  missteps but it successfully couches  grim truths and a tail with endearing  characters gorgeous art and moments of  jubilance and adventure making its tale  about how war destroys lives accessible  and even appealing to players of all  ages while still giving the war's  tremendous human cost the acknowledgment  it deserves the game begins by making it  clear that this isn't a simple tale of  good versus evil  Carl is a German citizen living in  France with his wife and newborn son but  as the war breaks out  he is forcibly separated from his family  and sent back to Germany where he must  join the war effort meanwhile his  father-in-law Emile is conscripted into  the French forces neither of them are  motivated to enlist or fight rather as  is so often the case in war they are  ordinary people who are swept up in  conflicts beyond their control  over the course of the game you play as  both emil and karl as well as a Belgian  nurse named Anna and an American soldier  named Freddie these characters aren't  traditional action heroes the older emil  for instance has to scramble and  struggle a bit to hoist himself over  obstacles and instead of running and  gunning their way through the game's  side-scrolling stages characters solve a  series of environmental puzzles to  proceed these puzzles are just  challenging enough to be engaging and  satisfying without being so difficult as  to interfere with the story's momentum  you do occasionally have to clobber an  unsuspecting enemy soldier from behind  and you may blast a few planes out of  the sky in one late-game scene but most  of your time is spent helping people  rather than attacking them in this game  you're not a killing machine the war  itself is there's an appropriate feeling  of futility that comes from charging  into battle again and again and seeing  soldiers on both sides fall in droves to  artillery blasts and machine gun fire  it's not all grimness and death  thankfully there are scenes of beauty  too like a sequence that takes place on  a starry night in Paris just as the war  is beginning here you play as the  headstrong and capable Anna a wonderful  character who is determined to do  whatever she can to help people during  the war after performing some quick  automotive repairs you drive down the  city's bustling streets and a joyous  scene during which you avoid cars and  other obstacles in keeping with the  music beautiful moments like this keep  the tone of the game from falling into  monotony and make the devastation of the  games grimmer scenes more impactful not  long after you leave the beauty of Paris  behind you're in the belgian town of eep  where the sky is filled not with  shimmering stars but with toxic gas  reinforcing the fact that lives on one  side aren't worth more or less than  lives on the other Anna rushes to assist  any injured soul she comes across  no matter the uniform he might be  wearing though the mechanics are simple  valiant hearts admirably puts you in a  wonderful variety of situations having  you do everything from cooking a meal  for a high-ranking officer to fighting a  boss battle against a Zeppelin using a  pipe organ as your weapon  no matter what you're doing the game's  art style pulls you in there are always  wonderful details in the background to  give the scenarios life and the designs  of the characters with their eyes  charmingly obscured by their hair endear  you to their struggles the game's  storytelling isn't as cohesive as it  should be for instance there's a jarring  disconnect between the French accented  voice we hear Emil used during gameplay  and the British accented voice that  speaks for him during between level  cutscenes rule has taken away a very  dear friend and on multiple occasions  the game leads you to think that a dire  fate has befallen one or more characters  only to reveal like the bad resolution  of a TV cliffhanger that this wasn't the  case but these are minor blemishes on a  beautiful game that ultimately doesn't  shy away from the fact that great is  just about the last thing any war should  be called  yes decision cannon firing enabled  Freddie and his regiment to reach the  rear  you  [Music]

